spec:
  grid: square, 7-27 rows/cols
  triples: 1-3 bar+segment+obstacle groups per grid; each uses 3 colors (may share across triples)
  bar:
    shape: straight line, 3-7 px, perpendicular to the edge it touches
    border: one endpoint on grid border, other endpoint (terminal) interior
    orientation: V (top/bottom border) or H (left/right border)
  segment:
    shape: 8-connected simple path (max degree 2, exactly 2 endpoints), 5-9 px
    attach: one endpoint 4-adjacent to bar terminal, perpendicular to bar direction
    direction: extends away from border into grid interior, 2-5 turns
    thickness: 1-cell-thick irregular stroke (no 2x2 blocks)
  obstacle:
    shape: small 4-connected sprite, 1-9 px, irregular (not always rectangular)
    position: tight against the inner side of the output segment's V apex; manhattan distance 2-6 from bar terminal
    fixed: unchanged between input and output
  transform:
    segment detaches from original position, re-routes to wrap tightly around obstacle (like a whip)
    output path (length L, 5-9) has 3 monotone phases (relative to bar's forward direction, i.e. away from border):
      phase 1 (approach): 0+ diagonal-forward steps toward obstacle from root side (FL if root is left, FR if right)
      phase 2 (alongside): 0+ straight-forward steps running alongside obstacle
      phase 3 (exit): 0+ diagonal-forward steps away on the opposite side (FR if phase1 was FL, vice versa)
      lengths of three phases roughly balanced (eval avg: ~ 2:1:2)
    no backward or lateral steps; phase transitions are strictly monotone (no mixing)
    segment does not pass through obstacle
    pixel count preserved (truncated if route hits grid boundary)
  colors: 3 per triple (all distinct within triple); bg is most-frequent color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N (7-27), bg color, number of triples T (1-3)
